      "html": "<p>Search for <strong>Care Inspectorate Wales compliance software</strong> and most results are English tools built around CQC. A Welsh care home answers to Care Inspectorate Wales, CIW, is registered and inspected under the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016, known as RISCA, and its regulations, and is expected to run an annual quality-of-care review with a Responsible Individual and manager accountable for ongoing compliance. Software that assumes the English system quietly steers a Welsh service towards the wrong evidence.</p><p>This page sets out the recurring audits a Welsh care home actually keeps on top of, expressed against Care Inspectorate Wales and Welsh law, and how quickler runs each as a WhatsApp workflow with no app. It also states plainly what quickler is <em>not</em>. For the equivalents across the British Isles, see <a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-uk.html\">care home compliance software UK</a>, <a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-scotland.html\">Scotland</a>, <a href=\"/pages/rqia-compliance-software-northern-ireland.html\">Northern Ireland</a> and <a href=\"/pages/hiqa-compliance-software-ireland.html\">Ireland</a>, and the <a href=\"/pages/five-regulators-one-job-british-isles.html\">five regulators, one job</a> essay for the wider picture.</p>"
