    "jsonld": "{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Article\",\n      \"headline\": \"Care Inspectorate Wales Compliance Software 2026\",\n      \"description\": \"Care Inspectorate Wales compliance software. Run the recurring audits behind a CIW inspection over WhatsApp under RISCA, self-assessed, one dashboard across services.\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"name\": \"Quickler Ltd\"\n      },\n      \"publisher\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"name\": \"Quickler Ltd\",\n        \"url\": \"https://quickler.co/\"\n      },\n      \"datePublished\": \"2026-08-28\",\n      \"dateModified\": \"2026-08-28\",\n      \"inLanguage\": \"en-GB\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n      \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What is Care Inspectorate Wales compliance software?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"It is software that helps a Welsh care home keep on top of the recurring audits behind a Care Inspectorate Wales inspection: medication management, infection prevention and control, safeguarding, falls and moving-and-handling, premises and fire safety, nutrition, care planning and governance, all self-assessed against the national standards and the quality-of-care framework under the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016, known as RISCA. Quickler does this as WhatsApp workflows with one dashboard across your services. It is not a care record or clinical system and holds no resident care data.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is this the same as CQC compliance software?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No. CQC and its four-word ratings apply in England only. In Wales the regulator is Care Inspectorate Wales, CIW, which registers and inspects under RISCA and its regulations and considers themes such as wellbeing, care and support, environment, and leadership and management. CIW does not use a numeric grade scale, so the evidence a Welsh service needs is different. Adult safeguarding is under the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014. See our care home compliance software UK, Scotland, Northern Ireland and Ireland guides for the other systems.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How does CIW judge a service, and does quickler award a grade?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Care Inspectorate Wales considers themes such as wellbeing, care and support, environment, and leadership and management, and describes its findings in general terms. It does not use a numeric grade scale, so always check current CIW guidance for the exact terminology. Quickler does not award or guarantee any judgement. It records your own honest self-assessment and the evidence behind it, so a real inspection confirms what you already know.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Does quickler replace our care records or eMAR system?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No, and it is not meant to. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer. For medication and care plans it records that the check was done and captures the evidence, without copying a resident's personal or clinical data into quickler. Personal plans, medication administration records and personal care logs stay in your care planning system, which remains the single source of truth. Quickler is not a care record, care management, eMAR or clinical system.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How does quickler handle Welsh-language duties and safeguarding in Wales?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Wales has its own Welsh-language duties, the Active Offer of Welsh-language care, and a service records how it meets Welsh-language needs. Quickler captures that evidence like any other observation, though it does not itself provide a Welsh-language feature. Adult safeguarding in Wales is under the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014, and quickler runs a periodic review that referrals, records and staff awareness are in order. Always work from the current published law.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is quickler affiliated with Care Inspectorate Wales?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No. Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by Care Inspectorate Wales, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. This page is general information, not regulatory advice, and you should always work from the current published standards and regulations.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\",\n      \"itemListElement\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 1,\n          \"name\": \"Home\",\n          \"item\": \"https://quickler.co/\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 2,\n          \"name\": \"Care Inspectorate Wales Compliance Software\",\n          \"item\": \"https://quickler.co/pages/care-inspectorate-wales-compliance-software.html\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"
